#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Examples of Cognitive Biases]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[Some common cognitive biases that affect financial decisions include:]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Overconfidence bias 🙇‍♂️]
#only("3-")[- Confirmation bias 🔍]
#only("4-")[- Loss aversion 📉]
#only("5-")[- Anchoring bias ⚓]
#only("6-")[- Herd behavior 🐑]
#only("1")[#voiceover("Let's look at some examples of cognitive biases that can lead to systematic errors in financial decision-making.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("Overconfidence bias is when individuals overestimate their own abilities, leading to excessive risk-taking.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("Confirmation bias is the tendency to search for, interpret, and remember information that confirms one's preconceptions.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("Loss aversion is the tendency to prefer avoiding losses rather than acquiring equivalent gains.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("Anchoring bias is the tendency to rely too heavily on the first piece of information encountered when making decisions.")]
#only("6")[#voiceover("And herd behavior is the tendency to follow and mimic the actions of a larger group, often ignoring individual analysis.")]
]

